        "status": "success",
        "rationale": "Each behavioral obligation in `requirements.sdk.filesystem-storage.interface` is covered by a marked test in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs`.\n\n1. **`new` retains the root and does not touch the filesystem.**\n   - `fn[paths_are_injective_and_loading_missing_records_has_no_side_effects]` builds the store over a missing root. It asserts that `record_path` equals `root.join(expected)` for every case. It asserts `!root.exists()` after the missing-record loads.\n   - `fn[send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys]` asserts `!root.exists()` right after `new`.\n\n2. **The store is `Send` and `Sync`.**\n   - `fn[concurrent_readers_only_observe_complete_records_from_competing_writes]` shares an `Arc<FileEvidenceStorage>` across scoped threads. That compiles only if the store is `Send` and `Sync`.\n\n3. **The `load` and `store` futures are `Send`.**\n   - `fn[send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys]` passes both futures through `fn send<T: Send>(value: T) -> T`. This is a compile-time check, which suits the obligation.\n\n4. **`Record`, `Dependency` and `Fingerprint` support Serde when their type parameters do.**\n   - `fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]` round-trips `Record<String, ()>` and `Record<String, String>`. It covers both `Dependency` variants, `Node` and `OutgoingEdges`, including a non-trivial label and the fingerprint. It asserts equality of version, dependencies and output after loading.\n   - The same test loads with incompatible parameters (`u8` for node data, `u8` for label) and expects `FileStorageError::Json`. That shows the bounds on the type parameters are really applied.\n\n5. **`Criterion::Ok` is always serializable, and its JSON value is already in the record.**\n   - The record's `output` is arbitrary JSON, including nested metadata. It round-trips equal in the round-trip test, the nested-path test and the concurrent test.\n\n6. **The SDK supplies `Record<D::NodeData, D::EdgeLabel>`, with serialization bounds applying to this helper.**\n   - `fn[consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path]` stores and loads through a graph, so the helper's record type is exercised with real node data.\n   - Bad JSON on load returns a `Json` error.\n   - The cited `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.persisted_dependencies` is context, and its own tests are not reassessed here.\n\nI found no unexercised obligation or missing marker."
