      "rationale": "Clause: \"The SDK supplies `Record<D::NodeData, D::EdgeLabel>` under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.persisted_dependencies`\". This prescribes the type of the record helper. `ValidationContext::finish` is that helper: it returns `Result<Record<D::NodeData, D::EdgeLabel>, serde_json::Error>`. A behavior-preserving alternative, such as a helper returning `Record<NodeId<D>, D::EdgeLabel>` or a private wrapper type that is serialized the same way, would break the clause. None of the supplied roots covers this signature. `Record`, `Dependency`, `Fingerprint`, `Criterion::Ok` and `FileEvidenceStorage` cover the other clauses: the Serde derives, the `Ok` bound, and the `Send`/`Sync` store and futures. `finish` is not reached from any of those roots, and it has no {impl} for the interface requirement."
    }
